WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:03.680
Every AI product sits on a data platform.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:08.090
So loops now ask data engineers to design the data side of AI.

3
00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:12.790
Three ideas: embeddings, RAG pipelines, and feature stores.

4
00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:14.625
First: embeddings.

5
00:00:14.645 --> 00:00:17.438
An embedding turns a text into a list of numbers.

6
00:00:17.458 --> 00:00:18.710
A vector.

7
00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:22.820
Texts with a similar meaning get vectors that sit close together.

8
00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:25.595
A vector index finds the nearest ones fast.

9
00:00:25.615 --> 00:00:28.670
It trades a little accuracy for speed.

10
00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:29.645
Second: RAG.

11
00:00:29.665 --> 00:00:31.405
Look it up, then answer.

12
00:00:31.425 --> 00:00:33.218
Split the documents into chunks.

13
00:00:33.238 --> 00:00:34.080
Embed them.

14
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.543
Retrieve the best ones.

15
00:00:35.563 --> 00:00:37.540
Then generate the answer.

16
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.165
Treat it like any pipeline.

17
00:00:39.185 --> 00:00:42.900
It must be incremental, versioned, and safe to run again.

18
00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:43.625
And measure it.

19
00:00:43.645 --> 00:00:45.325
Did we retrieve the right chunks?

20
00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:47.550
Was the answer correct?

21
00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:49.735
Third: features for a model.

22
00:00:49.755 --> 00:00:54.245
A feature store serves the same feature for training and for live requests.

23
00:00:54.265 --> 00:00:56.832
The trap is to train with data from the future.

24
00:00:56.852 --> 00:00:58.405
That is leakage.

25
00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:01.543
So join each row to the feature values known at that moment.

26
00:01:01.563 --> 00:01:03.580
Point in time.

27
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.990
Last: model calls cost money.

28
00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:07.152
Version the prompts.

29
00:01:07.172 --> 00:01:08.465
Cache repeated calls.

30
00:01:08.485 --> 00:01:10.990
And trace every request.

31
00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:14.075
Quick recap of AI for data engineering.

32
00:01:14.095 --> 00:01:15.563
Embeddings keep meaning.

33
00:01:15.583 --> 00:01:17.450
RAG retrieves, then generates.

34
00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:20.135
And features need point-in-time joins.

35
00:01:20.155 --> 00:01:23.255
Now start the first lesson below.
